Z||000006||kslish||01-10-2001||07:54 PM||||Sheesh, the only time I seem to have a grand in my hand is when I'm on the way to buy a Fiero, as oppossed to the other way around.  All of my Fiero's have been cash transactions, the Formula from Ohio (later sold to my Dad), my SC from the used car dealer at college and my GT last summer from a local seller.  Never been able to sell one to a stranger after putting my time and effort into restoring them (the Formula obviously stayed in "the family"), so I don't know exactly how you'll feel when you finally watch her drive away.  I'm sure the GT will be there to console you.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Ken S.<BR>'86 SC and '87 GT||||reg||1
